renovate: an update with nothing to commit isn't pending on the dashboard

processBranch returns `no-work` with no branch when an update turns out to
change nothing (a lock file refresh whose lock is already current). The
dashboard didn't know that and listed it under Other Branches, "pending",
every run of its schedule, though there's nothing a PR could bring. It
returns the same when its artifacts failed and left no files to commit,
which must stay listed, to be retried. processBranch now says which
(`upToDate`: nothing to commit, no branch, no artifact error), a run keeps
it on the branch, and the dashboard leaves out an update that's up to date.

